      "widgets_values": [
        "## About Krea 2 Turbo\n\n[Krea 2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2) (Krea, Qwen3-VL 4B text encoder): an aesthetic text-to-image model.\nTurbo is the 8-step distilled variant. Write full descriptive sentences and stay well under ~500 tokens: very long\nprompts produce black images.\n\n**Settings**: 8 steps, CFG 1, euler, simple, 1024×1024 (up to 2048×2048). The negative conditioning is zeroed: at CFG 1\na negative prompt has no effect, so the Generate tab shows none.\n\n## Image Bench\n\nThe node titles carry Image Bench markers:\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list |\n| `ib:pp` | Image Bench Prompt | prompt and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` | KSampler | seed, steps, CFG scale, sampling method, schedule type |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | — (LoRA exploration only) |\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list of the Generate tab, or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt.\nThe **Image Bench Prompt** node applies them and passes the prompt on without the tags.\n**Load LoRA** stays bypassed; LoRA exploration enables it for its runs and bypasses it again afterwards.\n\nThe size is that of **Empty Latent Image**.\n\n**Style LoRAs** ([Comfy-Org/Krea-2/loras](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/tree/main/loras), strength 1.0) need\ntheir trigger words in the prompt, e.g. `<lora:krea2_darkbrush:1> monochrome ink wash style`:\n\n| LoRA | Trigger words |\n|------|---------------|\n| `krea2_darkbrush` | `monochrome ink wash style` |\n| `krea2_dotmatrix` | `monochrome stippling style` |\n| `krea2_kidsdrawing` | `naive expressive sketch style` |\n| `krea2_neondrip` | `textured abstract style` |\n| `krea2_rainywindow` | `rainy window style` |\n| `krea2_retroanime` | `purple retro anime style` |\n| `krea2_softwatercolor` | `art deco watercolor style` |\n| `krea2_sunsetblur` | `ethereal motion blur style` |\n| `krea2_vintagetarot` | `vintage tarot style` |\n\nSet the trigger words as the activation text of a LoRA in the Explore tab, and the Generate tab adds them with its tag.\n\n## Model Links\n\nFor BF16 and NVFP4 variants, see [Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2).\n\n**diffusion_models**\n\n- [krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors)\n\n**text_encoders**\n\n- [qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors)\n\n**vae**\n\n- [qwen_image_vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_vae.safetensors)\n\n**loras**\n\n- [krea2_darkbrush.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/loras/krea2_darkbrush.safetensors)\n\n## Model Storage Location\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n└── 📂 models/\n    ├── 📂 diffusion_models/\n    │   └── krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors\n    ├── 📂 text_encoders/\n    │   └── qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors\n    ├── 📂 vae/\n    │   └── qwen_image_vae.safetensors\n    └── 📂 loras/\n        └── krea2_darkbrush.safetensors\n```\n\nKrea 2 is released under the Krea 2 Community License.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: Krea 2 Turbo",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
